Ultimate Weapons Structured Reference
This file reorganizes Ultimate Weapon knowledge into the same keyed mechanic format used by the Workshop source.
The original raw source remains preserved in public/knowledge/ultimate_weapons for side-by-side comparison.

Mechanic: Ultimate Weapons
Type: System
Category: Workshop
Aliases: uw
Disambiguation: This entry is about the Ultimate Weapons system itself, not an individual weapon's stat table, a single UW+ ability, or unrelated workshop stats.
Definition: Ultimate Weapons are workshop-owned systems purchased with Power Stones. Each unlocked Ultimate Weapon has three base upgrade stats, all owned Ultimate Weapons can run in the same round, and Ultimate Weapon Plus adds a second layer of upgrades after the full set is unlocked.
Formula:
Ultimate Weapon Damage = UW Multiplier * Core Module Multiplier * Damage * (1 + Critical Factor * Critical Chance) * (1 + Super Crit Mult * Super Crit Chance * Critical Chance).
Critical Ultimate Weapon Damage with Ultimate Crit = Ultimate Weapon Damage * Critical Factor.
Workshop:
Purchasing: Ultimate Weapons are bought with Power Stones. Each purchase shows 3 random remaining weapons with equal odds, and closing the menu without buying keeps the same offer.
Costs: 1st through 9th weapon costs are 5, 50, 150, 300, 800, 1250, 1750, 2400, and 3000 stones for 9705 total.
Usage: All owned and perk-granted Ultimate Weapons can run together in a round. They auto-activate when cooldown hits zero, and the cooldown resets immediately even if the previous activation is still active.
Toggle limit: Turning a UW off and back on resets its cooldown, and UWs can only be toggled 40 times in a run.
Enhancements: Ultimate Weapon Plus unlocks after all 9 base Ultimate Weapons are owned. Unlock costs increase by owned UW+ count: 500, 625, 750, 975, 1250, 1650, 2200, 2900, 3800. Each UW+ ability starts at level 0 and follows one of the documented cost trees.
Labs: Each weapon has its own lab support listed on the weapon entry.
Cards: Ultimate Crit can make damage-dealing Ultimate Weapons crit using workshop Critical Factor. It does not apply to % based damage.
Masteries: None.
Modules:
Core module substats directly modify named Ultimate Weapon stats and are listed on each weapon entry. Damage-dealing UWs also inherit shared Workshop-stat module boosts, so Cannon Critical Chance, Critical Factor, and Super Crit substats, plus other module effects that multiply tower damage, can raise UW damage through the shared formula.
Unique modules: Multiverse Nexus synchronizes Death Wave, Golden Tower, and Black Hole and sets their shared cooldown to the average of the three with Epic +20s, Legendary +10s, Mythic +1s, and Ancestral -10s. Galaxy Compressor, a Generator unique module rather than a Core unique module, also affects cooldown-based UWs by reducing their cooldowns by 10s, 13s, 17s, and 20s on package pickup at Epic, Legendary, Mythic, and Ancestral. Some weapons also take direct support from other module families, such as Space Displacer feeding Inner Land Mines.
Relics: Global relic bonus pool includes Ultimate Damage +35% total possible. Relic bonuses of the same type add together and multiply with other bonus families.
Vault: Power Vault contains four separate 5% Ultimate Weapon Damage nodes for +20% total global UW damage.
Perks: Unlock a Random Ultimate Weapon grants one currently unowned UW in a semi-upgraded form for the run, still takes applicable module substats, does not unlock labs, and leaves the perk pool once all UWs are owned. Weapon-specific UW perks only appear when that UW is unlocked or was granted by the random-UW perk, and they are: 4 More Smart Missiles, Swamp Radius x1.5, +1 Wave on Death Wave, Extra Set of Inner Mines, Golden Tower Bonus x1.5, Chain Lightning Damage x2, Chrono Field Duration +5s, Black Hole Duration +12.0s, and Spotlight Damage Bonus x1.5. Golden Tower Bonus x1.5 does not apply to the Golden Tower bonus submodule effect.
Footguns: Core module support does not mirror every base stat on every weapon. Use the current Core substat table when a Core stat list differs from the stone-upgrade stat list.

