Disambiguation: This entry is about Death Wave as an individual Ultimate Weapon, not the Ultimate Weapons system as a whole, another weapon, or the Kill Wall UW+ row in isolation.
Definition: Death Wave fires Effect Waves and then a persistent Death Wave driven by a damage pool. Effect Waves provide coin, health, cell, damage-amplification, and armor-stripping support before or alongside the damaging wave.
Basic Upgrades:
Basic upgrades for Death Wave are located in the Ultimate Weapon menu after unlocking the Ultimate Weapon. Unlocking Death Wave allows the player to upgrade Damage, Effect Wave Quantity, and Cooldown using stones.
Upgradeable stats:
• Damage
• Effect Wave Quantity
• Cooldown
Costs:
Damage has 30 levels.
Effect Wave Quantity has 4 levels.
Cooldown has 25 levels.
Total stones to max: 29,391.
Ultimate Weapon Plus:
Kill Wall causes each Effect Wave hit to amplify the Death Wave damage store additively.
Ultimate Weapon Plus abilities can only be unlocked once all 9 Ultimate Weapons are purchased.
Formula: Uses the global Ultimate Weapon damage formula with Death Wave Damage as the UW multiplier, but the wave persists until its stored damage pool is spent.
Behavior:
Core mechanics:
• The Death Wave is a single powerful wave that deals damage based on a damage pool.
• The damage pool accumulates damage through multiple activations rather than resetting with each new use.
• The damage pool only decreases by the exact amount required to destroy enemies, factoring in bonuses.
• The Death Wave remains active within tower range until the damage pool is depleted.
Effect Waves:
• Before the Death Wave strikes, it is preceded by a series of Effect Waves.
• Effect Wave Quantity is the stat formerly represented by Quantity and effectively functions like a duration because the animation is cosmetic while effects trigger immediately as waves are fired.
• Effect Waves have infinite range and occur at 4-second intervals.
Effect Wave utilities:
• Coin Bonus: Enemies hit by an Effect Wave or the Death Wave drop additional coins upon destruction.
• Health Bonus: Each enemy hit increases max health by 0.05% when destroyed.
• Cell Bonus: Elite enemies struck yield additional cells.
• Damage Amplification: Each Effect Wave hit increases the damage dealt by the Death Wave to that enemy. Starts at 5x at base.
• Armor Stripping: Effect Waves strip armor from enemies, reducing their defenses against the Death Wave.
Base stats: Damage x2 to x9,119, Effect Wave Quantity 1 to 5, Cooldown 300s to 50s.
Labs: Death Wave labs unlock at Tier 3 Wave 250 and cover Health, Coins Bonus, Cell Bonus, Damage Amplifier, and Armor Stripping.
Death Wave Health: Maximum health bonus from killing enemies marked or killed by Death Wave is increased, up to 12.5x base. Bonus health is tracked during a round by clicking on health in the workshop once at least one level is researched.
Death Wave Coins Bonus: Extra coin bonus applied to enemies hit by Effect Waves or killed by Death Wave. Has 20 levels.
Death Wave Cell Bonus: Extra cell bonus applied to enemies hit by Effect Waves or killed by Death Wave, up to 3x cell bonus. Has 20 levels.
Death Wave Damage Amplifier: Each Effect Wave hit on a given enemy boosts the damage that enemy takes from the Death Wave, up to +50x per Effect Wave. Has 30 levels.
Death Wave Armor Stripping: Each Effect Wave hit strips some amount of armor from an enemy, up to a max reduction of 10. Has 10 levels.
Cards: Ultimate Crit applies to the damage-dealing Death Wave because it scales from tower damage rather than % enemy health.
Masteries: None.
Modules:
Core module substats: Damage Common +8x, Rare +15x, Epic +25x, Legendary +50x, Mythic +100x, Ancestral +250x. Cooldown Legendary -6s, Mythic -10s, Ancestral -13s.
Unique modules: None dedicated to Death Wave in the Core family.
Perks: Unlock a Random Ultimate Weapon can grant a semi-upgraded Death Wave for the run; module substats still apply, but Death Wave labs stay locked. The random-perk version keeps the base health bonus, coin bonus, and damage amplification, but not the Cell Bonus or Armor Stripping features. +1 Wave on Death Wave adds one more Effect Wave. The weapon-specific perk only appears when Death Wave is already unlocked or was granted by the random-UW perk that run.
Footguns: Current Core substat data modifies Damage and Cooldown only; Effect Wave Quantity is not currently exposed as a Core substat.
Interactions: Multiverse Nexus synchronizes Death Wave with Golden Tower and Black Hole and sets their shared cooldown to the average of the three with a rarity-based modifier. Galaxy Compressor also reduces Death Wave cooldown by 10s, 13s, 17s, and 20s on package pickup at Epic, Legendary, Mythic, and Ancestral. Because Death Wave uses the shared UW damage formula, Cannon Critical Chance, Critical Factor, and Super Crit module substats, plus other module effects that multiply tower damage, also raise its real damage output. Global Ultimate Damage relics provide up to +35% total UW damage. Power Vault provides four separate 5% Ultimate Weapon Damage nodes for +20% total global UW damage.

